  "hints": [
    "An increasing path represents a combination without redundant permutations.",
    "After picking a value, only consider larger values in the next recursive call.",
    "Save at length k. Otherwise iterate choices only while enough larger values remain to finish the path.",
    "Undo the appended value after each recursive branch."
  ],
  "editorial": "Build strictly increasing paths. Starting the next call at chosen+1 prevents both repetition and reordering duplicates. If needed entries remain, the current choice can be at most n-needed+1; later choices cannot leave enough values to finish. Copy completed paths into the result. There are C(n,k) outputs of length k, with O(k) auxiliary recursion space.",
